On Sun, Jun 16, 2013 at 6:12 PM, Ian Johnson <blindbravado@gmail.com> wrote:

> On Sun, Jun 16, 2013 at 9:14 AM, selpa'i <seladwa@gmx.de> wrote:
>
>> ro mi'o = mi .e do
>
> While I agree with this suggestion (as we already discussed on IRC), I
> disagree with this equation. Instead ro mi'o = ro mi .e ro do. If the 3
> speakers together carry a piano and the 3 listeners together carry a piano
> then {mi .e do bevri lo pipno} is true while {ro mi'o bevri lo pipno} is
> false.
>
> mi'e la latro'a mu'o
>
Note that this statement is based on a {jo'u}-connected form of {mi'o},
which is not how the word is defined in CLL. Without this, {ro mi'o} is
almost always just {mi'o}, since there is typically only one mass of {mi'o}.

mi'e la latro'a mu'o

